---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "Gamaredon (Primitive Bear) APT
  Profile and MITRE ATT&CK Breakdown".

  Gamaredon is a Russia-aligned advanced persistent threat group active since
  2013, attributed to the Russian FSB. The group focuses on cyber espionage
  and data theft, primarily targeting Ukrainian government and defense
  sectors. They utilize custom malware families such as GammaLoad and
  GammaSteel alongside various obfuscation and persistence techniques.

  The rule chains 3 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 30min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule YAXTrTrvQXoi.
let $stages = {
  seq0: [
    "c550cc75-398e-4985-a1e9-5088e126e468", // Possible CVE-2025-8088 / CVE-2025-6218 (WinRAR Vulnerability) Exploitation Attempt (via file_event)
    "e70092a5-1b91-4a90-9a32-8b94307c9147", // Suspicious LOLBAS MSHTA Defense Evasion Behavior by Detection of Associated Commands (via process_creation)
    "bc139ef2-0c05-4cf7-b7af-3261d2cb2d68", // LOLBAS WScript / CScript (via process_creation)
    "5c411f93-3f10-4a48-bf16-20e7bea45769", // Call Suspicious .NET Classes/Methods from Powershell CommandLine (via process_creation)
    "4ab60adc-7117-4f20-80de-77ecf2a1ef99", // Call Suspicious .NET Methods from Powershell (via powershell)
  ],
  seq1: [
    "86576778-953f-45ee-a506-87f6cb12cef9", // Possible Persistence Points [ASEPs - Software/NTUSER Hive] (via registry_event)
    "a762e4b2-8596-4442-bd84-7ec5f224dc8a", // Schtasks Points to Suspicious Directory / Binary / Script (via cmdline)
    "27a5e681-d455-4567-be1f-f68e7c5d7449", // Suspicious Binary / Scripts in Autostart Location (via file_event)
    "ce152116-1d05-408a-a1a7-a4091528dc74", // An Archive Was Extracted To Suspicious Directory Using Powershell (via powershell)
  ],
  seq2: [
    "69b6437e-cee7-4b31-a02b-537356cff33d", // Download or Upload via Powershell (via cmdline)
    "4586d131-5d2a-4582-b028-a5841eea1d35", // Possible Dynamic DNS Service Was Contacted (via dns)
    "e0ee9a7b-fed3-4467-a012-0b04338e1334", // Possible Data Exfiltration over Rclone Tool (via cmdline)
  ],
}
sigma rules=[...$stages.seq0, ...$stages.seq1, ...$stages.seq2].map(uid => socprime::$rules[uid])
socprime::hos::chain uid="5b2823dd-1701-415f-a5cf-bd974d46d319",
  name="Gamaredon (Primitive Bear) APT Profile and MITRE ATT&CK Breakdown",
  level="high",
  tags=[],
  stages=$stages,
  timeframe=$timeframe,
  threshold=$threshold,
  tolerance=$tolerance
